<title>UK: Lockheed, Raytheon bidders for UK radar deal.</title>
<headline>Lockheed, Raytheon bidders for UK radar deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consortia led by Lockheed Martin Corp and Raytheon Co are to be invited to submit final offers for a 750 million stg contract for an ASTOR stand-off radar system for Britain's armed forces, defence procurement minister James Arbuthnot said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have decided to invite the two consortia to submit best and final offers for the full development, production and in-service support of ASTOR,&quot; he said in a written parliamentary answer.</p>
<p>&quot;We aim to place a contract with the winning consortium in 1998.&quot;</p>
<p>Arbuthnot said both consortia included British sub-contractors. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
